ices aren\'t properly configured to send metrics or traces. \n\nThe next step could be to check the dependency graph to see how the services are interconnected. If there\'s a service that\'s not properly connected or has a misconfigured dependency, that could cause issues. Using get_dependency_graph might reveal if there are any missing or incorrect service dependencies. \n\nAlso, since the metrics aren\'t showing up, maybe the services aren\'t exposing the necessary endpoints for Prometheus. Checking the services\' configurations or logs could help, but since the user can only use the provided tools, maybe the dependency graph can hint at which services might be problematic. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the issue is with the Jaeger setup itself. If the traces aren\'t being collected, that could be a problem. But the user already tried getting traces for one service and got nothing. Maybe checking the dependency graph would show if other services are involved that aren\'t being traced. \n\nSo, the best tool to use next is get_dependency_graph with a reasonable time frame, like the last 5 minutes, to see if there are any anomalies in the service dependencies that might indicate a problem.\n</think>\n\ntool name: get_dependency_graph  \nreasoning: The empty traces and missing metrics suggest potential issues with service communication or metric exposure. The dependency graph will reveal if services are properly connected and identify any broken links or misconfigured dependencies that could cause failures.  \n\ntool_call: {"last_n_minutes": 5}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=423, prompt_tokens=8302, total_tokens=8725, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff05-d0be-7512-8cfb-b6d58ce574de-0', tool_calls=[], in