l should be to check the deployments related to Jaeger. If there\'s no Jaeger deployment, that\'s the root cause. If there is a deployment but no pods, maybe there\'s a rollout issue. But given the previous results, the most likely issue is that Jaeger isn\'t deployed, leading to no traces and metrics being collected. Therefore, the answer would be that the Jaeger service is not properly deployed, causing the absence of traces and metrics.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The absence of Jaeger pods indicates that the tracing component is not running or misconfigured. To confirm this, I need to check if the Jaeger deployment exists and is healthy. If no Jaeger deployment is found, this would explain the lack of traces and metrics.  \n\ntool_call: {"command": "kubectl get deployments -n train-ticket -l app=jaeger"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=550, prompt_tokens=8900, total_tokens=9450, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff06-6b1d-7613-b043-2499da1ec6f4-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8900, 'output_tokens': 550, 'total_tokens': 9450}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='de8be656-6dde-4b98-a09c-c901f8e68406')]]
