So, the key issue seems to be that the Jaeger service isn't properly set up in the cluster. The Grafana dashboard might be misconfigured to show a service that doesn't actually exist. The absence of Jaeger components means there's no tracing data, and without metrics, it's hard to pinpoint performance issues. The user needs to verify if Jaeger is supposed to be part of the setup. If it's not, then the Grafana configuration is incorrect. If it is, then the deployment is missing, and they need to deploy it correctly. This misconfiguration is likely the root cause of the missing monitoring data.
