: {'arguments': '{"query": "sum by (job) (rate(http_requests_total{job!=\\"\\"}[5m]))"}', 'name': 'get_metrics'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-91876f434b6cc884', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 397, 'prompt_tokens': 8892, 'total_tokens': 9289, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff05-5955-7543-9161-38c703d6cac7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_metrics', 'args': {'query': 'sum by (job) (rate(http_requests_total{job!=""}[5m]))'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-91876f434b6cc884', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8892, 'output_tokens': 397, 'total_tokens': 9289}), ToolMessage(content='("{\'resultType\': \'vector\', \'result\': []}", 12)', id='efe7542d-cd77-4a0f-ad12-747a7fcae62f', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-91876f434b6cc884'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='5b359763-4f33-4d11-bd9b-974d332013d7'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose issues in the Train Ticket microservice application. So far, they\'ve checked the pods and deployments, and everything seems to be running normally. The next step was to look into metrics using Prometheus, but the initial queries didn\'t return any data. The user tried different queries, but they all came back empty.\n\nHmm, maybe the problem isn\'t with the pods or deployments but with the monitoring setup. If the metrics aren\'t being scraped, perhaps the Prometheus configuration is incorrect. Alternatively, the services might not be exposing the necessary metrics endpoints. Since the previous queries didn\'t find any metrics, it\'s possible that the services are